bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    jit_u64_array_push_high_bit_corruption_2026-11-27, 0, "Seed JIT: pushing a u64 >= 2^63 into a [u64] array stores it with bit 62 flipped; index stores, literals and [i64] pushes are exact. Broke Argon2id on the JIT once argon2 stopped demoting to the interpreter."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    jit_u64_array_push_high_bit_corruption_2026-11-27, P1, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "Seed JIT [u64].push flips bit 62 for values >= 2^63", src/lib/common/crypto/argon2.spl, 284, test/01_unit/lib/common/crypto/u64_array_push_high_bit_spec.spl, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    jit_u64_array_push_high_bit_corruption_2026-11-27, 0, "2026-11-27 reproduced on aarch64 DGX with seed cargo-target-wr-seed1126b (interpret exact, jit xor=0x4000000000000000). Workaround in src/lib/common/crypto/argon2.spl (pre-sized index-assigned [u64] buffers); RFC 9106 5.3 vector passes on both engines."
    jit_u64_array_push_high_bit_corruption_2026-11-27, 1, "2026-11-27 W8-3 root cause + fix: empty [u64] ignored expected_target_type/declared_elem_ty in HIR/MIR and allocated unpacked RuntimeArray via rt_array_new instead of rt_array_new_with_cap_u64; Cranelift maybe_packed_u64_store_word/load_word & data_at shifted unpacked u64 slots <<3/>>3 without HeapUInt boxing, and runtime unchecked/data_at omitted as_heap_u64(). Fixed HIR/MIR empty [u64] allocation, Cranelift boxed fallback (rt_value_u64/rt_value_as_u64), and runtime slot helpers; waiting-for: Rust seed rebuild."
